Spec: Java contract conformance runner

Purpose:
  Verify shared encoded inputs against independently declared expected outcomes and detect mutable model regressions.

Owns:
  ./ConformanceMain.java

References:
  /contracts/vectors/cases.json
  /docs/adr/0001-public-contract-normalization.md
  /contracts/java/src/main/java/dev/linkgate/contracts/ManifestContract.sdd

Must:
  Compare shared status/operation DTO cases and verify returned wire maps do not mutate retained values.
  Compare normalized objects structurally and fail the process when any accepted or rejected outcome differs.
  Write the aggregate and per-case results requested by the runner contract without printing rejected input values.
  Verify returned collections cannot mutate the parsed declaration and changing the input byte array cannot change it.
  Verify invalid input errors contain no input text or original parser cause.
  Evaluate shared connection request and separate approved-policy cases without treating a syntactically valid request as authorization.

Done when:
  All shared cases and immutable-model checks pass with Java compilation warnings treated as errors.
